        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-264857",
        ":question/problem": "Given the function $f(x,y;a,b)=axy+b,$ compute ${∇}_{a,b}\\,f.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">${∇}_{a,b}\\,f=\\text{ }$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
        ":question/worked-solution": "To compute ${∇}_{a,b}\\,f$, we take partial derivatives with respect to $a$ and $b.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂a} & =\\frac{∂}{∂a}(axy+b)=xy \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂b} & =\\frac{∂}{∂b}(axy+b)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{a,b}\\,f & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂a} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂b}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}xy \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      }
