      ":question/id": "1639c64c-655b-5822-8464-0f4a704887df",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "e-17534",
      ":question/problem": "Given the function $f(\\mathbf{x}; \\mathbf{w}) = (w_1x_1 - w_2+x_2)^2,$ compute $\\nabla_{\\mathbf{w}}(\\nabla_{\\mathbf{w}} \\: f).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we compute $\\nabla_{\\mathbf{w}} \\: f$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{1}}({w}_{1}{x}_{1}-{w}_{2}+{x}_{2})^{2}=2{x}_{1}({w}_{1}{x}_{1}-{w}_{2}+{x}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{2}}({w}_{1}{x}_{1}-{w}_{2}+{x}_{2})^{2}=-2({w}_{1}{x}_{1}-{w}_{2}+{x}_{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the second derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}^{2}}=2{x}_{1}^{2}\\,\\, &  & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}∂{w}_{2}}=-2{x}_{1} \\\\  & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}∂{w}_{1}}=-2{x}_{1}\\,\\, &  & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}^{2}}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}({∇}_{w}\\,f) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}∂{w}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}∂{w}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{1}^{2} & -2{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1} & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
