        ":question/id": "d8078445-7f57-54e9-9fc5-bfc3757a9189",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-264884",
        ":question/problem": "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}$, compute ${∇}_{x,z}({∇}_{x,z}\\,f).$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">${∇}_{x,z}({∇}_{x,z}f)=\\text{ }$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we take the variable subset gradient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x,z}\\,f & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2x \\\\ 2z\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the second derivatives with respect to $x$ and $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x)=2\\,\\, &  & \\frac{∂}{∂z}(2x)=0 \\\\  & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(2z)=0\\,\\, &  & \\frac{∂}{∂z}(2z)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x,z}({∇}_{x,z}\\,f) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂z} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂z∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{z}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
