        ":question/worked-solution": "To compute ${∇}_{x,y}\\,f$, we take partial derivatives with respect to $x$ and $y$ only.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y+y{z}^{2}) & =2xy \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y+y{z}^{2}) & ={x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x,y}\\,f & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2xy \\\\ {x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
